A||||4||fiero56||does anyone have this rare Fiero tranny||||5||
Z||000000||fiero56||05-25-2001||09:10 PM||||I am wondering if anyone here owns an '84 with the "economy" transmission(3.32 F/D), and drives it. I've got all the numbers in front of me, and on paper, it sounds like just the tranny I've been looking for. I am wondering how nice it drives for a daily driver. Are there empty spaces where there just isn't the right gear for given loads/speeds? ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Eric_PA||05-25-2001||10:44 PM||||I have that tranny in my 84. It's great on the higway, but can't seem to find a gear to drop down into when flying on the back roads. I find myself driving in third gear a lot around town.<P>Eric<BR>Black 86.5 GT Fastback ratmatic<BR>Red 84 4 speed||||reg||1
Z||000002||rockcrawl||05-26-2001||12:05 AM||||While we're on the subject of trannys, can anyone confirm these ratios? The ones in question are the '84 4:10 4 speed, and the '86 V6 4 speed. If correct, the M19 4.10 has about the same top end as the M17, but with a much lower first gear. I found another source that said the fourth (overdrive) gear is the same (.81) which would make this incorrect.<P>1984 L4 Final Drive 4.10 RPO M19  <BR>1st    2nd    3rd    4th     <BR>3.53   1.95   1.24   0.73        <P>1986 V6 3.65   M17<BR>3.31   1.95   1.24   0.81        <P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by rockcrawl (edited 05-26-2001).]||||reg||5
Z||000003||Songman||05-26-2001||03:07 AM||||All I know about it is that in my Indy first gear is almost worthless unless you are stopped at a red light on a hill... as soon as you get going you have to shift to second.<P>I also noticed that at about 80mph on the interstate I am around the 4000 rpm range. Guess this is okay if you are used to it, but I come from the V8 world. It drives me crazy! hehe... No way is this car good for cross country trips with that gear...<P>I'm about to get used to how close the gears are together. Don't know how much more difficult the short shifter is gonna be when I get one..<P>I'll be interested to watch and see if anyone has any info on these numbers.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000004||fiero56||05-26-2001||10:47 AM||||Hey rock,<P>The M19 and M17 both have .81 4th gear. The 3.32 has .73 4th gear. I've got the '86 V6 4-speed, and love it. It doesn't have a nice highway gear though. Its perfect for around town since the gears are spread apart(I don't like close ratio trannies). On the highway at 65mph(calculated, not real world tested), the '86 tranny spins the engine only about 366rpm less than the M19. But, the rpms will increase at a slower rate(as you speed up) due to lower final drive of the M17. At 100mph, there is almost a 500rpm difference between M19 and M17. But the 3.32 '84 tranny, will spin 1200 less than 4.10 at 100mph. My calculations are not perfect...yet.<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 05-26-2001).]||||reg||1
